flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a new repository starts
    accDescr: copier copy writes the files of the project and runs no code of the blueprint. python3 .github/blueprint.py create, which every copy brings, makes the first commit on the branch main with a sign-off, creates the repository with gh repo create and pushes to it, applies the settings as code and shows the checklist. You take the steps that only a person can take, such as the release app and the secrets, and then the checks and the bots run.

    copy(["`**copier copy**<br>the files of the project,<br>no code of the blueprint runs`"])
    commit["`**blueprint.py create**<br>git init on main,<br>the first commit, signed off`"]
    repo["`**gh repo create**<br>the repository, pushed`"]
    settings["`**settings apply**<br>rulesets, security,<br>environments, labels`"]
    checklist["`**checklist**<br>what is left for a person`"]
    you(["You: the release app<br>and the secrets"])
    bots["The checks and<br>the bots run"]

    copy --> commit --> repo --> settings --> checklist --> you --> bots

